<title>FRANCE: Accor sees higher 1997 results.</title>
<headline>Accor sees higher 1997 results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Accor chairman Jean-Marc Espalioux forecast a &quot;marked rise&quot; in net profit for 1997 and an increase of more than 20 percent in gross operating profit for the year.  </p>
<p>Espalioux made the forecast at the annual shareholders meeting on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The hotel group reported a gross operating profit of 1.52 billion francs last year and consolidated net attributable profit of 1.06 billion on sales of 28.31 billion.</p>
<p>He said results would rise despite the de-consolidation of Compass to whom it sold catering group Eurest.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
